# Loupe Layer 2 — protected-path CODEOWNERS template
# https://github.com/fadi-labib/loupe/blob/main/docs/reference/decisions.md#d-08
#
# The Action's PAT is scoped `contents: write` only on refs matching
# `loupe/proposal-*` — so the agent CANNOT push directly to main or to
# user PR branches. The mechanism: a fine-grained GitHub PAT supplied
# via the LOUPE_PAT secret. See data-handling.md for the full setup.
#
# CODEOWNERS is the second leg of Layer 2: even though the agent's
# pushes are confined to side branches, the sub-PRs those branches
# generate must NOT be merge-able into protected paths without explicit
# human approval. This file enforces that property at merge time, not
# at push time.
#
# Replace @your-org/security-reviewers with the team or user that
# should approve protected-path changes in your repo.

# Files the agent must never write directly.
# The agent uses propose_patch → .loupe/.proposed/ for these; a human
# applies them via `loupe chat`. Sub-PRs that contain changes to any of
# these need explicit security-reviewer approval before merge.
/.loupe/context.md          @your-org/security-reviewers
/.loupe/decisions/          @your-org/security-reviewers
/.loupe/config.yaml         @your-org/security-reviewers
/.loupe/knowledge.yaml      @your-org/security-reviewers

# OPTIONAL: stricter audit posture — gate ALL of .loupe/ under
# CODEOWNERS, requiring explicit reviewer approval for every Loupe
# sub-PR before merge. Trades adoption friction for audit signal.
# /.loupe/                  @your-org/security-reviewers
